      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under dry argon/glovebox conditions, tBuONa (2.88 g, 30.0 mmol) in THF (50 mL) was added to a suspension of NdCl3 (2.51 g, 10.0 mmol) in THF (50 mL). The mixture was stirred for 3 d at 25 °C, decanted overnight and filtered. Solvents were removed at 20 °C and the residue dried under 10−3 Torr for 6 h to give a pale blue solid (3.36 g, 82%). Crystals of 1·THF were grown from concentrated toluene at −5 to 5 °C. An alternative amide alcoholysis used tBuOH (3.0 mL, 31 mmol) and Nd[N(SiMe3)2]3 (1.25 g, 2.0 mmol) in THF (20 mL) for 3 d at room temperature, then recrystallization from toluene (0.48 g, 57%).",
